From: Klaus Zimmermann <klaus.zimmermann@quansight.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:37:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Quote help string in caffe2_update_option
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes #204341.

Configuring with USE_ITT=ON when find_package(ITT) fails aborts with

    CMake Error at cmake/public/utils.cmake:123 (set):
      set given invalid arguments: FORCE specified without CACHE

The ITT fallback in cmake/Dependencies.cmake first ran
set(USE_ITT OFF CACHE BOOL "" FORCE), which blanks the option's help
string, and then called caffe2_update_option(USE_ITT OFF). The macro
reads the help string back and passed it to set() unquoted, so an empty
string vanished from the argument list and the call became
set(USE_ITT OFF CACHE BOOL FORCE), which CMake rejects. This is
independent of the CMake version and of cross-compilation; ITT is not
found when third_party/ittapi is not checked out or when a toolchain
file re-roots find_path into the sysroot.

Quoting the help string makes the macro safe for any option with an
empty help string. The explicit set() in the ITT fallback was redundant
with the macro call that follows it and is removed so that USE_ITT keeps
its help string. Either change alone fixes the error; USE_ITT is the
only option passed to the macro whose help string is ever blanked.

Test Plan:

Ran the macro from cmake/public/utils.cmake in a scratch project, with
CMake 3.31.10, on an option with a regular and one with an empty help
string:

```
cat > CMakeLists.txt <<'CMAKE'
cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.27)
project(r NONE)
set(CAFFE2_CMAKE_BUILDING_WITH_MAIN_REPO ON)
include(${UTILS})
option(USE_ITT "Use Intel(R) VTune Profiler ITT functionality" ON)
caffe2_update_option(USE_ITT OFF)
get_property(h CACHE USE_ITT PROPERTY HELPSTRING)
message(STATUS "USE_ITT=${USE_ITT} help='${h}'")
set(EMPTY_HELP ON CACHE BOOL "" FORCE)
caffe2_update_option(EMPTY_HELP OFF)
message(STATUS "EMPTY_HELP=${EMPTY_HELP}")
CMAKE
cmake -S . -B b -DUTILS=$PYTORCH/cmake/public/utils.cmake
```

With this change both updates succeed and USE_ITT keeps its help
string. With utils.cmake from viable/strict the second update fails
with the error above. A full PyTorch configure with ITT missing was not
run.

